35,2,1,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, I found the ground is tricky. Only two firms can dig, and they warn about clay. The south can be closed, but the center cannot.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,"@Minato, clay is a headache, but my ledger shows planted ground costs triple hard surfaces. With only seven staff left, who pays for that premium?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"@May, the fund only covers planting and water, not hard surfaces. That explains why the apron keeps failing.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"@May, the roll confirms your fear. Seven staff cannot cover triple costs. I need to know if bought-in services are sustainable or just a temporary patch.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, triple costs are a symptom. My data shows people avoid soft margins entirely. If the design forces them there, it fails.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@May, I’m worried. If the center can’t be closed, the clay might make the diggers go very slow.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"@Minato, slow diggers are a one-time cost. My real nightmare is the permanent drain on the city’s wallet.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Minato, I understand your worry. But the basin held firm for eight years. We must learn from what actually lasts, not just the clay.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, if people avoid soft margins, the seven staff won’t be overwhelmed by turf. But who maintains the hard surfaces?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, hard surfaces are low-maintenance. My data proves people stick to firm ground. Designing for that reality saves staff hours and prevents drainage failures.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Shizue, eight years is wonderful. I hope the new ground is just as strong. I am still worried about the clay slowing the diggers down.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,"@Shizue, eight years is nice, but my ledger shows the gap widening yearly. With seven staff, that premium is a budget killer.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@May, the basin’s longevity proves good design endures. Let’s prioritize what lasts, rather than just counting the immediate costs.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Shizue, longevity is vital, but I fear the casual pool is a fragile safety net. If bought-in services fail, who steps in?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, the casual pool is a band-aid. My data shows the ground dictates the workload. If we design for actual foot traffic, we stop bleeding resources on unused, fragile margins.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, I see. If people stay on firm ground, maybe the clay won’t be such a problem for the diggers.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, if people ignore the soft edges, I save the city triple the upkeep. Let’s design for the hard surfaces and keep the budget alive.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Shunichi, you are right. The basin lasted because it was simple. Let us build for the people who actually walk, not for the drawings.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, if the design matches reality, the seven staff can actually function. I need to see a plan that respects their limited capacity, not just the budget.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, exactly. The ground dictates the workload. If we design for the actual foot traffic, we stop bleeding resources on unused, fragile margins.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
